Sogen: Xmm0-15 and MxCsr travel with CONTEXT_FLOATING_POINT

cpu_context::save and restore moved Xmm0-15 and MxCsr only under
CONTEXT_XSTATE. On x64 they are CONTEXT_FLOATING_POINT's: the SSE registers
overlay the legacy save area (FltSave), and CONTEXT_XSTATE adds only the AVX
state beyond them. An exception is dispatched with CONTEXT64_ALL, which has
FLOATING_POINT and not XSTATE, so its context carried no XMM registers and
the NtContinue that resumed the faulting code restored none: the code went on
with whatever XMM values the handler had left.

A runtime that resumes after faults on purpose meets that at once. SBCL's
Windows GC stops a thread by protecting its safepoint page, so every poll
faults and resumes; building nodecode, the main thread took 862 such faults
at 0x50100000 in 72 seconds, and the compiler then failed on arguments no
correct run produces:

  Unhandled SB-EXT:UNKNOWN-KEYWORD-ARGUMENT: Unknown &KEY argument: 0
  0: (SB-C::OPERAND-RESTRICTION-OK * #<SB-C:PRIMITIVE-TYPE :NAME T> 0 0)

Both directions now take the SSE state under either flag, and save fills
FltSave.MxCsr as Windows does. Every context the emulator builds itself
(thread start, APC, exception) is saved from live registers whose MXCSR is
set first, so none restores a zero MXCSR.

diff --git a/src/windows-emulator/cpu_context.cpp b/src/windows-emulator/cpu_context.cpp
index edad0b4..9df55f2 100644
--- a/src/windows-emulator/cpu_context.cpp
+++ b/src/windows-emulator/cpu_context.cpp
@@ -6,6 +6,19 @@ namespace sogen
 
     namespace cpu_context
     {
+        namespace
+        {
+            // On x64, Xmm0-15 and MxCsr are CONTEXT_FLOATING_POINT's, with the x87 area they overlay (FltSave);
+            // CONTEXT_XSTATE adds only the AVX state beyond them. Read under CONTEXT_XSTATE alone, they were
+            // in no context an exception is dispatched with (CONTEXT64_ALL), so the NtContinue that resumes
+            // the faulting code left it whatever XMM values the handler had put there.
+            bool carries_sse_state(const CONTEXT64& context)
+            {
+                return (context.ContextFlags & CONTEXT_FLOATING_POINT_64) == CONTEXT_FLOATING_POINT_64 ||
+                       (context.ContextFlags & CONTEXT_XSTATE_64) == CONTEXT_XSTATE_64;
+            }
+        }
+
         void restore(x86_64_cpu& emu, const CONTEXT64& context)
         {
             if ((context.ContextFlags & CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS_64) == CONTEXT_DEBUG_REGISTERS_64)
@@ -69,7 +82,7 @@ namespace sogen
